<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Florence</h1><p class="st-meta">1532 CE – 1569 CE · capital Florence</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Medici duchy, created by Charles V in 1532, under which Cosimo I conquered Siena and turned Florence into a princely state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the siege of 1529–1530 ended the last <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-florence">Republic of Florence</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Charles V</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-de-medici">Alessandro de' Medici</a> hereditary duke in 1532. Alessandro ruled with the support of imperial troops and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fortezza-da-basso">Fortezza da Basso</a> to control the city.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-de-medici">Alessandro</a> was murdered by his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzino-de-medici">Lorenzino</a> in 1537, and the 17-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> was chosen to succeed him. Cosimo crushed the republican exiles at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-montemurlo">Montemurlo</a> that year and built an efficient absolutist state. He founded the Uffizi offices, designed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giorgio-vasari">Giorgio Vasari</a> from 1560, created a navy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-saint-stephen-tuscany">Order of Saint Stephen</a>, and conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-siena">Republic of Siena</a> in 1555.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1569 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-v">Pope Pius V</a> raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-of-tuscany">Grand Duke of Tuscany</a>, and the duchy became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Grand Duchy of Tuscany</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-florence.jpg" alt="Duchy of Florence" width="320" height="373"><figcaption>Image: Heralder · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Augmented_Arms_of_Medici.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1532 CE – 1569 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Florence</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alessandro de' Medici, Cosimo I de' Medici</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tuscan Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Florence</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1550&amp;focus=duchy-of-florence" aria-label="Duchy of Florence on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4950 627 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Florence lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5270 883L5270 883M5270 883L5229 694M5270 883L5270 883M5270 883L5273 897M5270 883L5277 905"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5270 883h0M5229 694h0M5270 883h0M5273 897h0M5277 905h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5270 883h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5270 883h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Florence. <a href="/atlas?year=1550&amp;focus=duchy-of-florence">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
